.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The contract carries `perso` material (Operator's own words). The app NEVER writes it to
# disk -- if a capture is ever taken one day for debugging, it does not end up
# in the history. We ignore the WHOLE DIRECTORY: a file dropped there tomorrow
# is protected by default, without anyone having to think about it.
captures/

# What the server said at the start of the RUNNING run -- read by `lancer.command`
# to find the address to open. A machine trace, never part of the history.
.journal/
